363 Section 6. Section 78A-2-704 is amended to read:
364 78A-2-704. Public policy regarding attorney guardian ad litem -- Training.
396 (1) An attorney guardian ad litem may not presume that a child and the child's parent are adversaries.
398 (2) An attorney guardian ad litem shall be trained on and implement into practice:
399 (a) the parental rights and child and family protection principles provided in Section 80-2a-201;
401 (b) the fundamental liberties of parents and the public policy of the state to support family unification to
the fullest extent possible;
403 (c) the constitutionally protected rights of parents, in cases where the state is a party;
404
- 14 -

HB0372S03 compared with HB0372S04
(d) the use of a least restrictive means analysis regarding state claims of a compelling child welfare
interest;
406 (e) the priority of maintaining a child safely in the child's home, whenever possible;
407 (f) the importance of:
408 (i) kinship placement, [in the event] if the child is removed from the home;[ and]
409 (ii) keeping sibling groups together, whenever practicable and in the best interests of the children;
380 (g) { and}
411 {(iii) {understanding and communicating the minor's expressed interests to the court;}
412 {(g)} the preference for kinship adoption over nonkinship adoption, if the parent-child relationship is
