771 80-2-301. Division responsibilities.
772 (1) The division is the child, youth, and family services authority of the state.
773 (2) The division shall:
774 (a) administer services to minors and families, including:
775 (i) child welfare services;
776 (ii) domestic violence services; and
777 (iii) all other responsibilities that the Legislature or the executive director of the department may assign
to the division;
779 (b) provide the following services:
780 (i) financial and other assistance to an individual adopting a child with special needs under Sections
80-2-806 through 80-2-809, not to exceed the amount the division would provide for the child as a
legal ward of the state;
