1296 Section 13. Section 80-3-104 is amended to read:
1297 80-3-104. Individuals entitled to be present at proceedings -- Legal representation --
Attorney general responsibilities.
987 (1)
(a) A minor who is the subject of a juvenile court hearing, any person entitled to notice under Section
80-3-201 or 80-3-301, preadoptive parents, foster parents, and any relative providing care for the
minor, are:
990 (i) entitled to notice of, and to be present at, each hearing and proceeding held under this chapter,
including administrative reviews; and
992 (ii) have a right to be heard at each hearing and proceeding described in Subsection (1)(a)(i).
994 (b) A child's right to be present at a hearing under Subsection (1)(a) is subject to the discretion of
the guardian ad litem appointed under Subsection (3) or the juvenile court regarding any possible
detriment to the child.
997 (2)
(a) The parent or guardian of a minor who is the subject of an abuse, neglect, or dependency petition
has the right to be represented by counsel, and to present evidence, at each hearing.
1000 (b) If a parent or guardian is the subject of an abuse, neglect, or dependency petition, the juvenile court
shall:
1002 (i) appoint an indigent defense service provider for a parent or guardian determined to be an indigent
individual in accordance with Title 78B, Chapter 22, Part 2, Appointment of Counsel; and
1005 (ii) order indigent defense services for the parent or guardian who is determined to be an indigent
individual in accordance with Title 78B, Chapter 22, Part 2, Appointment of Counsel.
1008 (3)
(a) In an abuse, neglect, or dependency proceeding under this chapter, the juvenile court shall order that
the child be represented by an attorney guardian ad litem, in accordance with Section 78A-2-803.
1011 (b) A guardian ad litem appointed under Subsection (3)(a) shall represent the best interest of the minor,
in accordance with the requirements of Section 78A-2-803:
1013
- 49 -

