(i) at the shelter hearing and at all subsequent court and administrative proceedings, including any
proceeding for termination of parental rights in accordance with Chapter 4, Termination and
Restoration of Parental Rights; and
1016 (ii) in other actions initiated under this chapter when appointed by the court under Section 78A-2-803 or
as otherwise provided by law.
1018 (4) Subject to Section 67-5-17 and the attorney general's prosecutorial discretion in civil enforcement
actions, the attorney general shall, in accordance with Section 80-2-303, enforce this chapter,
